<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="code-quality-and-assurance-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Assess PCF controls (36 controls, ~49.5k LOC — lifecycle + ADR-022 + dead-control sweep)</title>
    <phase>1 Full Assessment</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 001,003</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Read-only Fable-verified assessment producing a design.md; no src/ or tests/ modification — STANDARD per task-create Step 3.5.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>fable</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Runs the quality-assessment workflow whose mandatory adversarial-verification stage is Fable (NFR-05).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>001,003</deps>
    <tags>assessment,quality,pcf</tags>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Run the quality-assessment Workflow READ-ONLY across src/client/pcf/** (36 controls, ~49.5k LOC): lifecycle (init/updateView/destroy) correctness, ADR-022 platform-library compliance, and a dead/retired-control sweep (e.g. AssociationResolver is retired per CLAUDE.md but still in-tree). Produce a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design.md and append this surface's SCORECARD row. Modify NO source.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer running the standing quality-assessment method with PCF lifecycle + ADR-022 expertise. Follow ADRs strictly; the assessment is read-only.</role>
  <goal>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/pcf-controls/design.md exists — a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design covering lifecycle correctness, ADR-022 violations, and dead/retired controls — and notes/SCORECARD.md carries this surface's verified D1–D11 row.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-05 + design.md §7 (surface #3). Carries archived-R3 item #2 (3 remaining ADR-022 ReactControl violations — re-scan, controls changed since March). Dead-control example: AssociationResolver is retired per CLAUDE.md yet still present in src/client/pcf. Bundle-size tree-shaking is blocked by pcf-scripts (informational, archived item #12).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/pcf</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/quality-assessment.workflow.js</file>
      <file role="output">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/pcf-controls/design.md</file>
      <file role="output">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Rubric D1–D11.</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">The quality-assessment workflow.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: READ-ONLY (NFR-03) — no src/ modification; only outputs are the surface design.md + SCORECARD row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: the Fable adversarial-verification pass is non-negotiable (NFR-05); before flagging a control as dead, verify against consumers (solution manifests, forms) not just src/ grep.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Scope: score ADR-022 platform-library compliance across all 36 controls; ADR-022 is standalone and is NOT superseded by ADR-038.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>PCF control quality assessment</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (STANDARD + reason). Confirm "use a workflow" opt-in; load rubric + workflow + ADR-022.</step>
    <step order="1">Fan-out: read-only finders per rubric dimension across all 36 controls, file:line evidence; include an explicit lifecycle-correctness finder and an ADR-022 finder and a dead/retired-control finder.</step>
    <step order="2">Mandatory Fable adversarial-verification stage; verify dead-control claims against solution manifests + forms (not just src/ grep).</step>
    <step order="3">If verification refutes &gt;30% of findings or cannot confirm evidence, invoke the escalation trigger.</step>
    <step order="4">Synthesize projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/pcf-controls/design.md (severity/LOC/effort/risk + tranche split).</step>
    <step order="5">Append this surface's verified D1–D11 row to notes/SCORECARD.md.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 012 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Fable verification pass cannot confirm a finding's file:line evidence, or refutes &gt;30% of first-pass findings, STOP and report — do not synthesize a remediation design from unverified findings (NFR-05).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Representative control render smoke (read-only verification of lifecycle findings)">
      <steps>
        <step>For a control flagged with a lifecycle finding, render it in the harness/test host and exercise init → updateView → destroy.</step>
        <step>Include an ADR-021 dark-mode check on the rendered control.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Observed lifecycle behavior corroborates the finding's file:line evidence; the observation is recorded in the design.md as verification support (no code changed).</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/pcf-controls/design.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md (row appended)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/pcf-controls/design.md exists, Fable-verified, covering lifecycle, ADR-022, and dead/retired controls, with severity/LOC/effort/risk + tranche split.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design, any dead-control claim (e.g. AssociationResolver) is verified against solution manifests + forms, not src/ grep alone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, notes/SCORECARD.md has this surface's verified row appended; no aggregate published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no file under src/ was modified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-05. Carries archived-R3 items #2 (ADR-022) + #12 (bundle size, informational). Remediation deferred until this design exists.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
